# Summary
Introduced a DoS risk by adding an unbounded reclaim queue and enqueuing on every payload lease drop without limits or rate control.
This commit moves payload reclamation to a background queue. The new queue stores (bucket, key, generation) tuples in a VecDeque/HashSet without any size limits or backpressure. Every payload lease drop enqueues an entry, even when there is no reclaim record, meaning high-volume reads across many objects can continuously grow the queue faster than the single worker can drain it. An authenticated (or anonymous on public buckets) client can issue many GETs/updates to create unique generations and force the queue to grow until memory exhaustion, causing a denial of service.

